(1) Notwithstanding anything contained in any other law for the time being in force, any dispute touching the constitution, election of the office bearers, conduct of general meetings, management or business of a society shall be referred by any of the parties to the dispute, or by a federal society to which the society is affiliated, or by a creditor of the society, to the Registrar, if both the parties thereto are one or other of the following :
(a) a society, its committee, any past committee, any past or present officer, any past or present agent, any past or present servant or nominee, heir or legal representative of any deceased officer, deceased agent or deceased servant of the society, or the liquidator of the society ;
(b) a member, past member or a person claiming through a member, past member or a deceased member of a society, or a society which is a member of the society ;
(c) a person, other than a member of the society, who has been granted a loan by the society, or with whom the society has or had transactions under the provisions of
Section 45
